Creating and Analyzing Disk Images Using dc3dd and Autopsy
Step 1: Start Kali Linux
Boot your Kali Linux VM
Log in and open terminal:
Ctrl + Alt + T

Step 2: Create Sample Evidence
Create a file that will later be found during analysis:
echo "Cybersecurity Lab Evidence" > evidence.txt
Verify:
ls

Step 3: Identify Disk Partition
List available storage devices:
lsbl
Example:
sda
├─sda1
├─sda2
👉 Note the partition (e.g., /dev/sda1)
⚠️ In real forensics, this is the target disk

Step 4: Install dc3dd (if not installed)
sudo apt update
sudo apt install dc3dd

Step 5: Create a Forensic Disk Image
✅ Correct Command (IMPORTANT)
sudo dc3dd if=/dev/sda1 of=/home/kali/disk_image.dd hash=md5 log=/home/kali/acquisition.log
Explanation
if= → input file (source disk/partition)
of= → output file (image file)
hash=md5 → generates hash
log= → saves acquisition details

Step 6: Verify Image Creation
Check image:
ls -lh /home/kali/disk_image.dd
View log:
cat /home/kali/acquisition.log
✔ Log contains:
Image size
Hash value
Acquisition details
Step 7: Verify Hash Manually (Optional but Recommended)
md5sum /home/kali/disk_image.dd
👉 Compare with hash in log file
✔ If both match → integrity confirmed

Step 8: Start Autopsy
Run:
autopsy
Open browser and go to:
http://localhost:9999/autopsy

Step 9: Create New Case in Autopsy
In the interface:
Click Create New Case
Enter:
Case Name: Disk Investigation
Description: Forensic Analysis Experiment
Click Next

Step 10: Add Host
Click Add Host
Enter:
Host Name: KaliLabMachine
Description: Kali Linux forensic machine
Click Next → Finish

Step 11: Add Disk Image
Click Add Image
Browse and select:
/home/kali/disk_image.dd
Click Next → Finish
Autopsy will begin analysis.

Step 12: Analyze Evidence
1. File System
Go to File Views → File System
Locate:
evidence.txt
Open and verify content

2. Keyword Search
Use Keyword Search
Enter:
Cybersecurity
View matching results

3. Deleted Files
Go to Deleted Files
Check recoverable files

4. Metadata Analysis
Check:
Created time
Modified time
File size

5. Extract Evidence
Right-click file → Extract File
Save for reporting

Final Result
Disk image successfully created
Hash verified (data integrity ensured)
Evidence file located in Autopsy
Analysis of files and metadata completed
